  "chapter": 608,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 17 Chapter 608\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 5399, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring the\n        department  of  health  to  conduct  a  public  information  and\n        outreach campaign on medically unnecessary treatments on persons\n        born with intersex traits or variations in sex characteristics\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would require the Department of Health to  conduct  a\npublic  information  and  outreach  campaign on the physical, sexual and\npsychological impact of medical procedures performed on  intersex  indi-\nviduals. While developing the outreach program, the Department of Health\nwould  consult with stakeholders including intersex people, intersex-led\norganizations, and their chosen advocates.\n \n  I am supportive of this bill, the first of  its  kind  in  the  United\nStates.  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to ensure that\nthis  outreach  program  is  developed  and delivered in an engaging and\nrespectful manner that includes appropriate stakeholders.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
